---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { money, site } from "../config";

const mail = `mailto:${site.contactEmail}`;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description={`The rules for using the hosted ${site.name} service: trial, payment, cancellation, refunds, and data deletion.`}
  updated={site.legalUpdated}
>
  <p>
    These terms are an agreement between you and {site.operator} ("we", "us"), who runs the hosted {site.name}{" "}
    service at <strong>app.rakumi.app</strong>. When you create an account or use the service, you agree to
    these terms and to our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. The service and the open-source code</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name} is a kitchen app for meal plans, pantry, recipes, cooking, and shopping. The source code is open
    source under the MIT license. If you run the code on your own server, the MIT license applies and these terms
    do not. These terms cover only the hosted service that we run for you.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Your account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You must be at least 13 years old. If you are under 18, a parent or guardian must agree to these terms.</li>
    <li>Give a real email address that you can read. We use it for sign-in, account warnings, and billing.</li>
    <li>Keep your password and API tokens secret. You are responsible for what happens in your account.</li>
    <li>
      Each account is for one household. The person who creates it is responsible for everyone who uses it,
      and for the AI assistants and tools they connect to it.
    </li>
    <li>Verify your email within 7 days. If you do not, you cannot use the app until you verify it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Free trial</h2>
  <p>
    New households get a {site.trialDays}-day free trial. You must add a payment card at checkout to start it.
    Each person can get one free trial. If you cancel before the trial ends, we do not charge you. If you do not
    cancel, your plan starts when the trial ends and we charge the card.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Price and payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The plan costs {money(site.price.monthly)} per month or {money(site.price.yearly)} per year, per household,
      plus any tax that applies.
    </li>
    <li>Your plan renews automatically at the end of each period until you cancel.</li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://polar.sh">Polar</a> is the merchant of record. Polar sells you the subscription, takes the
      payment, handles tax, and sends receipts. <a href="https://polar.sh/legal/terms">Polar's terms</a> also apply
      to your purchase.
    </li>
    <li>If we change the price, we will email you at least 30 days before your next charge at the new price.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Cancellation</h2>
  <p>
    You can cancel at any time. In the app, open <strong>Settings</strong>, then select <strong>Manage billing</strong>.
    You keep access until the end of the period you paid for. Then your household locks (see section 7).
  </p>

  <h2>6. Refunds</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      If you are not happy, you can get a full refund of your <strong>first</strong> charge. Email{" "}
      <a href={mail}>{site.contactEmail}</a> within 7 days of that charge.
    </li>
    <li>When we refund you, we also cancel the plan. Your household locks at once.</li>
    <li>We do not give refunds for later charges or for unused parts of a period, unless the law requires it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Locked households and data deletion</h2>
  <p>Your household locks when your plan ends, when a payment fails, or when we refund you.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>When a household is locked, you can still log in and start a plan again. You cannot use the app until you do.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>30 days after the lock, we permanently delete the household, its accounts, and all its data.</strong>{" "}
      We send warning emails before we delete it. After deletion, we cannot get the data back. Copies in our backups
      are deleted within 14 days after that.
    </li>
    <li>To keep a copy, email us before the 30 days end. We will send you your data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Your content</h2>
  <p>
    What you add to {site.name}, such as recipes, image links, notes, and plans, stays yours. You give us
    permission to store, copy, and show it only as needed to run the service for you. Add only content that you
    have the right to use.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Do not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Break the law or the rights of others with the service.</li>
    <li>Try to get into other households' data or our systems.</li>
    <li>Overload the service, for example with automated requests far above normal use.</li>
    <li>Resell the hosted service or share one plan between separate households.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If you break these rules, we can lock or close your account. If it is not urgent, we will email you first and
    give you time to fix the problem.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Food, nutrition, and health</h2>
  <p>
    Nutrition values, expiry dates, and dietary rules in {site.name} are estimates to help you plan. They are not
    medical, dietary, or food-safety advice. Always check labels, allergens, and whether food is safe to eat.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>
    One independent developer runs {site.name}. We work to keep it available and to back up data, but we do not
    promise that the service is always available or free of errors. We can add, change, or remove features. If
    we stop the hosted service, we will email you at least 30 days before, offer a copy of your data, and refund
    any unused prepaid time.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Disclaimer</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, we provide the service "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any
    kind, express or implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and
    non-infringement.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Limit of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive
    damages, or for lost data, profits, or revenue. Our total liability for any claim about the service is
    limited to the amount you paid us in the 12 months before the claim.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We will update the date at the top when these terms change. If a change is important, we will email you at
    least 14 days before it takes effect. If you continue to use the service after that, you accept the new terms.
    If you do not accept them, cancel your plan.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Law</h2>
  <p>
    The laws of the State of Maryland, USA, apply to these terms, without regard to conflict-of-law rules. Courts
    in Maryland decide any dispute, unless the law where you live gives you the right to go to your local courts.
  </p>

  <h2>16. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {site.operator}, Maryland, USA. Email <a href={mail}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
